package refarm:http-plugin-fixture@0.1.0;

// Test fixture world: a refarm plugin that ALSO imports wasi:http's
// outgoing-handler (an outbound HTTP client). This is the interface the
// `network:outbound` grant gates. The host builds two linkers — one WITH
// add_only_http_to_linker_async (granted), one WITHOUT (linker_no_http). A
// plugin that imports outgoing-handler links only against the http-capable
// linker; under Strict without the grant, this import fails to resolve and the
// load errors. That is what this fixture proves end-to-end.
//
// It still exports the canonical `integration` interface (like every plugin),
// so the host's load path is unchanged — only the extra wasi:http import
// distinguishes it from null-plugin.
world http-plugin {
    include plugin:host/refarm-plugin@0.1.0;
    import wasi:http/outgoing-handler@0.2.3;
}
